  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustaining the Gains of the Women, Peace and Security in the Philippines</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed Project seeks to sustain the gains of the Women, Peace and Security (WPS) Agenda in the Philippines through initiatives geared towards the institutionalization and mainstreaming of the WPS agenda across national and regional platforms and policies. These include technical and operational assistance for the recently-launched WPS Center of Excellence under the Office of the Presidential Adviser on Peace, Reconciliation and Unity (OPAPRU), the Diploma Course on Women, Peace and Security under the Mindanao State University-Maguindanao, the BARMM Gender and Development (GAD) Code, and reintegration programs for women formerly associated with armed groups.</narrative>
  </description>
